Id: cont003f
Severity: FAIL
Category: containers
Check: check_containers
References: https://docs.docker.com/engine/security/protect-access/
Controls: CIS 4.1, 5.4; NIST AC-6, CM-7; ISO 8.2, 8.9; CE Secure configuration, User access control

The Docker daemon listens on TCP (a tcp:// host in
/etc/docker/daemon.json or on dockerd's command line) without TLS
client verification (tlsverify). Anyone who can reach the port, 2375
by convention, can start a privileged container and is root on the
host; scanners look for that port on the internet all the time.

To fix it, remove the tcp:// host and use the Unix socket, reach a
remote daemon over SSH ('docker -H ssh://user@host'), or turn on
tlsverify with a CA, a server certificate and client certificates.
